{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TLContentStratification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TLContentStratification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_ne_zero_iff_length_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_ne_zero_iff_length_le","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TLContentStratification.lean#L148-L155","doc":"**The `N < 0` mirror.**  At `X = Q^{|N|}` (i.e. `Q^{-N}` with `N < 0`) the\nsurviving blocks are those with at most `-N` rows — the textbook\n`GL(N)`/HOMFLY form of the level-rank truncation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_eq_zero_iff_numCols_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_eq_zero_iff_numCols_gt","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TLContentStratification.lean#L141-L146","doc":"**Dropped blocks (`N ≥ 0`).**  The blocks removed at `X = Q^{-N}` are\nexactly those with strictly more than `N` columns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_ne_zero_iff_numCols_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_ne_zero_iff_numCols_le","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TLContentStratification.lean#L130-L139","doc":"**The Temperley–Lieb quotient, explicitly (`N ≥ 0`).**  At the physical\nMarkov parameter `X = Q^{-N}` with `Q > 1`, the Schur element of a\npartition `lam` **survives iff `lam` has at most `N` columns**.  Combined\nwith the cited `SchurElementCriterion`, the surviving Wedderburn blocks of\n`H_n(Q)` at `X = Q^{-N}` are exactly `{lam ⊢ n : lam₁ ≤ N}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.numCols_and_length_of_hasContentCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.numCols_and_length_of_hasContentCell","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TLContentStratification.lean#L122-L126","doc":"A content-`N` cell forces both bounds simultaneously. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.hasContentCell_iff_lt_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.hasContentCell_iff_lt_length","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TLContentStratification.lean#L109-L113","doc":"**The `N < 0` stratification (row form).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.hasContentCell_of_lt_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.hasContentCell_of_lt_length","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TLContentStratification.lean#L96-L107","doc":"**Hard direction (needs positive parts).**  With more than `-N` rows, the\ncell `(-N, 0)` exists — its row is nonempty because parts are positive —\nand has content `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.lt_length_of_hasContentCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.lt_length_of_hasContentCell","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TLContentStratification.lean#L88-L94","doc":"**Easy direction (no hypothesis on `lam` or `N`).**  A content-`N` cell\nsits in row `i = j - N ≥ -N`, so `lam` has more than `-N` rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.hasContentCell_iff_lt_numCols","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.hasContentCell_iff_lt_numCols","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TLContentStratification.lean#L80-L84","doc":"**The `N ≥ 0` stratification (column form).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.lt_numCols_of_hasContentCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.lt_numCols_of_hasContentCell","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TLContentStratification.lean#L66-L78","doc":"**Hard direction (needs weak decrease; holds for every `N`).**  A\ncontent-`N` cell forces more than `N` columns: the cell sits in some row\n`i` at column `j = N + i ≥ N`, and that row is bounded by the first.  Note\nno sign hypothesis on `N` is needed here — it is only the *converse* that\nrequires `0 ≤ N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.hasContentCell_of_lt_numCols","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.hasContentCell_of_lt_numCols","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TLContentStratification.lean#L53-L64","doc":"**Easy direction (no hypothesis on `lam`).**  If `lam` has more than `N`\ncolumns then cell `(0, N)` realises content `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.row_le_numCols","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.row_le_numCols","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TLContentStratification.lean#L42-L49","doc":"For a weakly decreasing partition every row is bounded by the first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.numCols","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.numCols","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TLContentStratification.lean#L34-L36","doc":"The number of **columns** of `lam`, i.e. its first (largest) part.\n`0` on the empty partition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}